Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["KnoodleIdentify", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"7a1a4cee-1bc2-437e-999c-0b84b383cb6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"ac77db7a-ca9c-49f0-b13c-b2c9be5700b5"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"KnoodleIdentify", "[", 
   StyleBox["input", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ce88c780-a480-40e3-a1f3-1f5d0cea6853"],
 "\[LineSeparator]identifies the knot type of a knot diagram by looking it up \
in Knoodle's knot lookup table (KLUT)."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d8743791-f06e-4407-b9ff-4253a55aaafd"],

Cell["\<\
KnoodleIdentify returns an Association from each identified prime summand, a \
KnotSymbol[c, i, alternating, coset], to its integer multiplicity. A connect \
sum of several prime knots gives one entry per distinct prime factor, with \
the factor's multiplicity as the value. The unknot gives <||>, the empty \
association: an unknot summand is the identity element for connect sum, so it \
is simply omitted.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"81afcfa2-d4e2-4470-a5b3-28c298a7158f"],

Cell["\<\
input accepts the same representations as KnoodleDraw. The lookup is \
self-contained: it decomposes and simplifies internally, so input need not be \
simplified first.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4efa08a2-9e37-4341-92cf-81fc3c9bd43f"],

Cell["\<\
A summand with more crossings than the lookup covers (the table's 13, or \
\"MaxCrossings\") comes back as Unidentified[n, pd] -> multiplicity, where pd \
is the summand's own signed PD code, for offline analysis. A summand inside \
the lookup range that still fails to resolve comes back as NotFound[n, pd] -> \
multiplicity instead, with a KnoodleIdentify::notfound warning: it points to \
a gap in the tables or a hard simplification case.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"99c45f7f-9391-48d1-9ab1-c6ea2adf73ff"],

Cell["\<\
If knoodleidentify itself fails -- for instance because its KLUT tables are \
missing, damaged or from another table set -- KnoodleIdentify returns $Failed \
with a KnoodleIdentify::knoodletool message quoting the tool's error.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bab264cc-8047-4c02-92fb-c0ee2eb111fa"],

Cell["\<\
KnoodleIdentify only identifies knots. A genuine link (more than one \
component) fails with $Failed and a KnoodleIdentify::link message; apply \
KnoodleSimplify with \"Unite\" -> True first if the components should be \
treated as connect-summed into a single knot.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"076d1e97-9e50-44d4-8599-61230a8d783f"],

Cell["\<\
3D geometry is projected to a diagram as in KnoodleDraw and KnoodleSimplify: \
after a uniformly random rotation by default, or straight down one axis with \
\"Projection\" -> \"X\", \"Y\" or \"Z\". The projection is exact, so even a \
highly symmetric curve viewed along an axis projects correctly. \
\"ExactInput\" -> True refuses floating-point coordinates that would have to \
be rounded onto Knoodle's integer grid, and RandomSeeding seeds the random \
projection and the Reapr embeddings tried during escalation (all but the bend \
randomization of their planar layout).\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1033f72b-7c01-484d-b9ca-89501ccb3425"],

Cell["\<\
KnoodleIdentify always tells knoodleidentify where the paclet's own KLUT \
tables are, so an environment variable or a separate Knoodle installation \
cannot substitute other tables. The tool checks the tables against the \
manifest shipped with them before every run.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fa491ec4-e548-40b9-922f-f6b159110edb"],

Cell["The following options can be given:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d305e2eb-8d4c-4592-83b1-2e8b0a9a0fa9"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "02d1a9bd-5def-4014-b8d8-3aaa27725c46"], "\"\<MaxCrossings\>\"", 
    "Automatic", Cell["\<\
restrict the lookup to subtables with at most this many crossings (3 to 13); \
Automatic is the table's full range. Knots above a restricted range come back \
as Unidentified.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d7356196-fff5-4341-a9f6-791ad6294568"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "30047ba7-06a1-4388-ac1f-3b9fad3930a1"], "\"\<Projection\>\"", 
    "Automatic", Cell["\<\
how 3D input is projected to a diagram: \"X\", \"Y\" or \"Z\" straight down \
that axis, \"Random\" after a uniformly random rotation; Automatic is \
\"Random\", or \"Z\" when \"RandomizeProjection\" -> False\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"530e0012-d101-4b9a-b17f-2d4917e10570"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ca3eda67-c1e0-4750-ab12-2e712956f42b"], "\"\<RandomizeProjection\>\"", 
    "True", Cell["\<\
the older switch for \"Projection\": False projects straight down the z axis\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"facfc837-28e8-4961-bb00-af3f518dbdfb"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "40d38308-89d8-4b61-a830-e2b4d9ab41af"], "\"\<ExactInput\>\"", "False", 
    Cell["\<\
True refuses 3D input that cannot be projected exactly, instead of rounding \
it onto an integer grid\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"edccc4a0-22f3-42eb-9fcc-6035461067fa"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6eb54414-bdde-461d-b975-4fee067814ae"], "RandomSeeding", "Automatic", 
    Cell["\<\
seed for the tool's random choices: an integer or string, Inherited to follow \
SeedRandom, or Automatic for a fresh seed every call\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5e5bda29-6ca4-416f-9591-ec7dec6c641b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "51d0a329-2c96-4063-a4a8-b6e4ff8415eb"], "\"\<IdentifyOptions\>\"", 
    RowBox[{"{", "}"}], Cell["\<\
extra knoodleidentify flags, e.g. {\"escalation-rounds\" -> 6, \"reapr-energy\
\" -> \"Height\"}; see knoodleidentify --help\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e9d55733-11a6-439a-8f02-a2e2b37569cd"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"a19ed92f-ca4f-4538-85f9-\
92b33cb1784a"]
}, Open  ]],

